# Copy to .env.local (gitignored). Never commit real values.

# The team folder. Default: crew/ in the folder the conductor starts in.
# CREW_TEAM_DIR=

# Overrides the team's store (shopify.store in crew.config.ts).
# SHOPIFY_STORE=

# Where Crew keeps its data (SQLite, session folders, engine sign-ins). Default: ~/.crew
# CREW_HOME=

# Conductor port. Default: 4317
# CREW_PORT=4317

# DEV ONLY: use your personal Claude Code / Codex sign-in instead of Crew's own
# engine folders. Agents may then see personal skills and settings. Off by default.
# CREW_SHARED_ENGINE_HOME=1

# A team server (see docs/server-briefing.md and deploy/):
# Fixed app token, the same across restarts (at least 32 characters).
# CREW_TOKEN=
# Cloudflare Access in front of the conductor: every request must carry a valid
# Access login for this team domain and application AUD tag.
# CREW_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# CREW_ACCESS_AUD=
# Who may sign tools in from the app on a server (comma-separated emails).
# CREW_ADMINS=
# Chromium for the browser connection where agent-browser has none (Linux ARM).
# AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=

# Code agents (permissions 'code'), see README → Safety:
# A GitHub App installed on the team's code repo with Contents and Pull requests
# read/write. Without one, Crew uses `gh auth token` (a developer's own Mac).
# CREW_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# CREW_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/home/crew/.crew-github-app.pem
# Theme Access password for theme_preview (else the Shopify CLI's own sign-in).
# SHOPIFY_CLI_THEME_TOKEN=

# Meta ads (@crew/kit/meta): an access token for Meta's Ads MCP server. A user
# token, or an Employee-role system user token (Admin-role is refused), with
# ads_mcp_management + ads_read, and ads_management for changes.
# META_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# DataForSEO (@crew/kit/dataforseo): the API login and API password from
# app.dataforseo.com → API Access (not the account password).
# DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=
# DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=

# Google Search Console (@crew/kit/search-console): a Google Cloud service
# account's JSON key, the whole JSON or base64 of it (one line is safest:
# `base64 -i key.json | tr -d '\n'` on a Mac, `base64 -w0 key.json` on Linux).
# Setup, once:
# 1. Google Cloud console → pick or create a project → IAM & Admin → Service
#    accounts → Create service account (no roles needed).
# 2. APIs & Services → Library → "Google Search Console API" → Enable.
# 3. The service account → Keys → Add key → Create new key → JSON.
# 4. Search Console → the property (e.g. sc-domain:example.com) → Settings →
#    Users and permissions → Add user → the service account's email
#    (…@….iam.gserviceaccount.com), permission Restricted.
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_KEY=
